  "question": {
    "text": "Modern vacuum pumps can evacuate a vessel down to a pressure of <math> <mrow> <mtext>4.0</mtext> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>5</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;atm. at room temperature (300 K). Taking R = 8.3 JK<sup>-1</sup>&nbsp; mole<sup>-1</sup>, 1 atm = 10<sup>5</sup> Pa and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mtext>Avogadro</mtext> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>6</mn> <mo>&#215;</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </msup> <msup> <mo>mole</mo> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math>, the mean distance between molecules of gas in an evacuated vessel will be of the order of :",
